From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:05:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: debayer_egl: Compute stats on the centred window

DebayerEGL::configure() sets the statistics window to Rectangle(window_.size()),
i.e. an output-sized rectangle anchored at (0, 0) of the raw frame. That is
correct for DebayerCpu, which feeds SwStatsCpu one line at a time from inside
the centred window, but the EGL path hands SwStatsCpu the whole mapped input
buffer through processFrame(), so the (0, 0) anchor makes AGC and AWB measure
only the top-left corner of the sensor image. On a 4032x3024 sensor with a
1280x960 output that corner is roughly 10% of the frame, so the displayed image
is exposed and white-balanced for whatever happens to be in that corner.

Pass the centred window (with its x/y offset) instead, matching what the
frame actually shows.

Observed on Google Pixel 3a (IMX363, simple pipeline, LIBCAMERA_SOFTISP_MODE=gpu):
AGC kept raising exposure on a blown-out frame because the corner was dark.
---
 src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
@@ -339,11 +339,8 @@
 	window_.width = outputCfg.size.width;
 	window_.height = outputCfg.size.height;
 
-	/*
-	 * Don't pass x,y from window_ since process() already adjusts for it.
-	 * But crop the window to 2/3 of its width and height for speedup.
-	 */
-	stats_->setWindow(Rectangle(window_.size()));
+	/* processFrame() sees the whole input buffer, so keep the window offset. */
+	stats_->setWindow(window_);
 
 	inputBufferCount_ = inputCfg.bufferCount;
 	outputBufferCount_ = outputCfg.bufferCount;
